  "responseText": "{\"reviewedAffectedSlots\":[\"W185\"],\"findings\":[\"W185 (nnxyz nnotb #14): The correctly composited image over white canvas reveals a substantially different visual character than the prior description captured. The background is not a soft pink field with background circles pulling against figure density. Instead, the upper zone is a warm peach-to-orange gradient with large, luminous white-edged circles (bokeh-like forms) that read as translucent overlays against the pink-tinged upper left. The figures are not simply oval heads with dissolving white vertical streaks: they are tall, elongated shroud-like forms — each head rendered in yellow, blue, magenta and white linework with open mouths showing teeth, eyes rendered as dark ovals or rings, bodies trailing downward as long semi-transparent white and multicolored streaks that reveal the warm background through them. The lower register is a dense black serrated band of upward-pointing spike or flame shapes outlined in white, which reads as a crowd or ground mass pressing up from below. The overall palette is warm pink, peach, orange, yellow, cyan and magenta — far more chromatic and layered than 'soft pink background circles' suggests. The translucency of the figure bodies is a genuine optical feature now visible against white: the streaks are not opaque white but layered semi-transparent washes through which background color shows. The previous description understated the chromatic intensity and mischaracterized the background as passive circles rather than active luminous overlapping forms.\"],\"membershipConcerns\":[],\"corrections\":[{\"slot\":\"W185\",\"whyHere\":\"Six elongated shroud-like figures rise in a loose row, each head built from yellow, cyan, magenta and white linework with a wide-open mouth and dark oval eyes; their bodies trail downward as long semi-transparent streaks through which warm peach and orange background tones remain visible. A dense black serrated band of spike forms lines the bottom edge, pressing upward against the figures. Large luminous white-edged circles float across the upper zone, overlapping the pink and peach ground. The image holds both the ordered row of the chapter and a layered translucency that keeps the figures from fully solidifying.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"The previous work placed five faces against a near-black ground, their jagged rings sharpening every edge; here the ground opens into warm peach and pink, and the figures' bodies become semi-transparent, so the row of heads is legible but the forms beneath them dissolve into the background color rather than holding firm.\"}],\"chapterCorrections\":[]}",
